 "notes": "Multiplayer challenge browser. TABS: 'Rooms' is SELECTED (warm brown fill, glowing gold frame, gold icon and warm-yellow label); Daily, Featured, Saved and Squad are inactive (dark navy fill, thin brass frame, grey-white icon and label). The selected tab's glow makes it 1px taller at the bottom. BRIEFING BAR (selected challenge summary): route picture well, map icon + route name, hairline separator, modifier skull icon + modifier name over a row of three difficulty skulls (first two gold/lit, third grey/unlit = difficulty 2 of 3), second hairline separator, a recessed code field (ticket icon + challenge code), and a slate LOAD button. ROOM LIST: three rows. Row 1 is HIGHLIGHTED/selected: glowing orange-gold frame (about 6px outer glow beyond the rect), a gold primary JOIN button with dark label, and a green READY chip (lit green dot + green label; the chip fades out to the right). Rows 2 and 3 have plain brass frames, slate JOIN buttons with light labels, and a hollow grey ready dot (not ready, no label). Each row: gold number tab over the top-left of a scene picture, a crest banner hanging over the picture (its rod with arrow finials sticks out ~13px either side of the banner rect), player-count icon above 'n / max', unit slots (filled slots show unit portraits, empty slots a grey plus), a side banner repeating the crest, the ready indicator and JOIN. Row 1 has 2 slots (79 and 76 wide, 1 filled); rows 2-3 have 4 slots 67 wide (2 and 3 filled). Faint vertical hairline dividers sit at about x435, x532, x850 and x931 inside each row. BOTTOM BAR: BACK, REFRESH, MATCH, HOST are slate secondary buttons with icons (BACK sits 3px lower than the others); START CHALLENGE is the parchment-gold primary with crossed swords. All button/chip labels are uniform full-caps Cinzel. Digit tabs are tall narrow numerals in the concept, so width-fitted sizes render shorter than the concept digits."
